# path:key  reason. key is a const name, or the offset call the check printed.
crates/desk/src/screens/accounts/mod.rs:POP_WIDTH  popover width, fits the 470 px area at the minimum window with the sidebar open
crates/desk/src/screens/accounts/mod.rs:top(px(POP_TOP))  popover anchored under its trigger, not a board coordinate
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/chrome.rs:BOARD  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/chrome.rs:left(px(left))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/chrome.rs:top(px(6.0))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/chrome.rs:top(px(POP_TOP))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/chrome.rs:top(px(top))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/page.rs:top(px(60.0))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/browser/page.rs:top(px(cursor_top))  whole-window mock-up, refit is its own ticket
crates/desk/src/modules/chat/mod.rs:CONTENT_WIDTH  max width of the transcript column
crates/desk/src/modules/file_edits/mod.rs:TILE_WIDTH  preferred tile width handed to the tiling layout
crates/desk/src/modules/shells/mod.rs:TILE_WIDTH  preferred tile width handed to the tiling layout
crates/desk/src/modules/subagents/mod.rs:TILE_WIDTH  preferred tile width handed to the tiling layout
crates/desk/src/modules/data_studio/side.rs:left(px(96.0))  popover anchored beside its trigger, outside DESK-194 owns
crates/desk/src/modules/data_studio/side.rs:top(px(36.0))  popover anchored beside its trigger, outside DESK-194 owns
crates/desk/src/modules/git/history.rs:top(px(40.0))  popover anchored under its trigger
crates/desk/src/screens/context/mod.rs:LINE_WIDE  ContextLine viewbox width, scaled to bounds by charts.rs
crates/desk/src/screens/frame.rs:outer_card  frame::panel, one of several side-by-side sections inside a tile, such as the Limits subscription cards
crates/desk/src/screens/session/mod.rs:outer_card  count(): the stat cards that sit side by side in a row inside the tile
crates/desk/src/screens/usage/mod.rs:outer_card  count(): the stat cards that sit side by side in a row inside the tile
crates/desk/src/screens/classifier/ledger.rs:inner_card  one inner card per decision-point panel and one in the ledger panel, sections inside the tile
crates/desk/src/screens/context/mod.rs:inner_card  the Context panels side by side, and their loading skeletons
crates/desk/src/screens/library/agents.rs:inner_card  the agent list panel and the agent detail panel, side by side
crates/desk/src/screens/session/mod.rs:inner_card  the stat cards, the turns and detail panels, and their loading skeletons
crates/desk/src/screens/settings/intro.rs:inner_card  the Background and Preview sections side by side on ISET-3
crates/desk/src/screens/usage/mod.rs:inner_card  the usage panels and stat cards side by side
crates/desk/src/screens/settings/mod.rs:shell  open() only picks a board: rows.rs frames ISET-1 with frame::tile, intro.rs frames ISET-3
crates/desk/src/screens/platforms/mod.rs:shell  per-OS window chrome reference kept in the dev build only (milestones.md, 2026-10-08), it draws a whole window
crates/desk/src/screens/intro/mod.rs:shell  first-run hero over a full-window picture, drawn before any tile exists
crates/desk/src/screens/onboarding/mod.rs:shell  first-run hero over a full-window picture, drawn before any tile exists
crates/desk/src/screens/accounts/mod.rs:outer_card  one of the side-by-side account columns inside the window tile (max_w COLUMN_SHARE), not a frame around the screen
